# EditMode Test Generation Standards

This file defines mandatory EditMode test generation standards for Spellwright. EditMode tests are fast, synchronous unit tests that validate ECS components, queries, and logic in isolation without Unity's game loop.

> **Note**: For integration tests requiring Unity runtime and frame updates, see `playmode-tests-generation.mdc`.

## Core Principles

EditMode tests are:

- **Synchronous**: Execute immediately without frame delays
- **Fast**: Complete in milliseconds
- **Isolated**: Test components and logic without full ECS infrastructure
- **Editor-only**: Run exclusively in Unity Editor
- **Deterministic**: Same input always produces same output

Use `[Test]` attribute (not `[UnityTest]`) for all EditMode tests.

## When to Use EditMode Tests

**Use EditMode Tests For:**

- Component data validation
- Entity creation and manipulation
- EntityCommandBuffer playback logic
- Component queries and filtering
- Pure logic without Unity services (Input, Physics, Time)
- Tag component behavior

**Example scenarios:**

- "Does this prefab have all required components?"
- "Does ECB.Instantiate create an entity after playback?"
- "Does the query return only validated requests?"

## Test Naming Convention

**Format**: `MethodUnderTest_Scenario_ExpectedBehavior`

**Examples:**

```csharp
SpawnRequest_WithValidPrefab_CreatesEntity()
InvalidPrefab_MissingSpeed_FailsValidation()
ECB_AfterPlayback_InstantiatesEntity()
Query_WithValidatedTag_ReturnsOnlyValidated()
Component_HasCorrectValue()
```

## Test Structure

```csharp
using NUnit.Framework;
using Unity.Entities;
using Unity.Mathematics;
using Unity.Collections;
using Unity.Transforms;

namespace Spellwright.Tests.EditMode.Systems.Spawning
{
    [TestFixture]
    public class SpellSpawnSystemTests
    {
        private World _world;
        private EntityManager _entityManager;

        [SetUp]
        public void SetUp()
        {
            _world = new World("TestWorld");
            _entityManager = _world.EntityManager;
        }

        [TearDown]
        public void TearDown()
        {
            if (_world != null && _world.IsCreated)
            {
                _world.Dispose();
            }
        }

        [Test]
        public void SpawnRequest_WithValidPrefab_CreatesEntity()
        {
            Entity prefab = CreateValidPrefab();
            Entity request = CreateSpawnRequest(prefab);

            Assert.IsTrue(_entityManager.Exists(request));
        }

        private Entity CreateValidPrefab()
        {
            Entity prefab = _entityManager.CreateEntity();
            _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new Speed { Value = 10f });
            _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new Lifetime { Duration = 5f });
            return prefab;
        }

        private Entity CreateSpawnRequest(Entity prefab)
        {
            Entity request = _entityManager.CreateEntity();
            _entityManager.AddComponentData(request, new SpawnRequest
            {
                PrefabEntity = prefab
            });
            return request;
        }
    }
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. World Management

**Always create and dispose test worlds:**

```csharp
[SetUp]
public void SetUp()
{
    _world = new World("TestWorld");
    _entityManager = _world.EntityManager;
}

[TearDown]
public void TearDown()
{
    if (_world != null && _world.IsCreated)
    {
        _world.Dispose();
    }
}
```

### 2. Entity Creation Helpers

**Create reusable helper methods:**

```csharp
private Entity CreateValidPrefab()
{
    Entity prefab = _entityManager.CreateEntity();
    _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new SpellOwner { OwnerEntity = Entity.Null });
    _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new Speed { Value = 10f });
    _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new Lifetime { Duration = 5f });
    return prefab;
}

private Entity CreateInvalidPrefab_MissingSpeed()
{
    Entity prefab = _entityManager.CreateEntity();
    _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new SpellOwner { OwnerEntity = Entity.Null });
    _entityManager.AddComponentData(prefab, new Lifetime { Duration = 5f });
    return prefab;
}
```

### 3. Testing EntityCommandBuffer

**Test after playback, use queries for validation:**

```csharp
[Test]
public void ECB_AfterPlayback_InstantiatesEntity()
{
    Entity prefab = CreateValidPrefab();
    var ecb = new EntityCommandBuffer(Allocator.TempJob);

    ecb.Instantiate(prefab);
    ecb.Playback(_entityManager);
    ecb.Dispose();

    int entityCount = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Speed)).CalculateEntityCount();
    Assert.AreEqual(2, entityCount);
}

[Test]
public void ECB_AfterPlayback_SetsComponent()
{
    Entity prefab = CreateValidPrefab();
    Entity caster = _entityManager.CreateEntity();
    var ecb = new EntityCommandBuffer(Allocator.TempJob);

    Entity deferredSpell = ecb.Instantiate(prefab);
    ecb.SetComponent(deferredSpell, new SpellOwner { OwnerEntity = caster });
    ecb.Playback(_entityManager);
    ecb.Dispose();

    var query = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(SpellOwner));
    var entities = query.ToEntityArray(Allocator.Temp);

    bool foundCaster = false;
    foreach (var entity in entities)
    {
        if (entity != prefab && entity != caster)
        {
            SpellOwner owner = _entityManager.GetComponentData<SpellOwner>(entity);
            if (owner.OwnerEntity == caster)
            {
                foundCaster = true;
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    entities.Dispose();

    Assert.IsTrue(foundCaster);
}
```

### 4. Component Validation

**Direct component checks:**

```csharp
[Test]
public void Prefab_HasAllRequiredComponents()
{
    Entity prefab = CreateValidPrefab();

    Assert.IsTrue(_entityManager.HasComponent<SpellOwner>(prefab));
    Assert.IsTrue(_entityManager.HasComponent<Speed>(prefab));
    Assert.IsTrue(_entityManager.HasComponent<Lifetime>(prefab));
}

[Test]
public void Speed_HasCorrectValue()
{
    Entity prefab = CreateValidPrefab();

    Speed speed = _entityManager.GetComponentData<Speed>(prefab);

    Assert.AreEqual(10f, speed.Value);
}
```

### 5. Query Testing

**Test query behavior:**

```csharp
[Test]
public void Query_WithValidatedTag_ReturnsOnlyValidated()
{
    Entity validRequest = CreateValidatedSpawnRequest();
    Entity invalidRequest = CreateSpawnRequest();

    var query = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(
        typeof(SpawnRequest),
        typeof(ValidatedTag)
    );

    int count = query.CalculateEntityCount();

    Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
}
```

### 6. NativeContainer Disposal

**Always dispose NativeContainers:**

```csharp
[Test]
public void Query_ReturnsCorrectEntities()
{
    CreateTestEntities();

    var query = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Speed));
    var entities = query.ToEntityArray(Allocator.Temp);

    Assert.AreEqual(3, entities.Length);

    entities.Dispose();
}
```

## Anti-Patterns

### 1. Don't Test Systems Directly

**BAD: Systems need full ECS infrastructure**

```csharp
[Test]
public void System_UpdateOnce_ProcessesRequests()
{
    var system = _world.GetOrCreateSystem<SpellSpawnSystem>();
    var systemState = _world.Unmanaged.ResolveSystemStateRef(system);
    system.OnUpdate(ref systemState);
}
```

**GOOD: Test component logic or use PlayMode for system integration**

```csharp
[Test]
public void ComponentLogic_Validates()
{
    Entity prefab = CreateValidPrefab();
    bool isValid = _entityManager.HasComponent<Speed>(prefab);
    Assert.IsTrue(isValid);
}
```

### 2. Don't Use ComponentLookup in EditMode

**BAD: ComponentLookup requires SystemAPI**

```csharp
[Test]
public void BadLookupTest()
{
    var lookup = _entityManager.GetComponentLookup<Speed>();
}
```

**GOOD: Use EntityManager directly**

```csharp
[Test]
public void GoodComponentTest()
{
    Entity entity = CreateValidPrefab();
    Speed speed = _entityManager.GetComponentData<Speed>(entity);
    Assert.AreEqual(10f, speed.Value);
}
```

### 3. Don't Access Deferred Entities

**BAD: Trying to access entity before ECB playback**

```csharp
[Test]
public void BadDeferredEntityTest()
{
    var ecb = new EntityCommandBuffer(Allocator.TempJob);
    Entity deferredEntity = ecb.Instantiate(prefab);

    Assert.IsTrue(_entityManager.Exists(deferredEntity));

    ecb.Dispose();
}
```

**GOOD: Use queries after playback**

```csharp
[Test]
public void GoodPlaybackTest()
{
    var ecb = new EntityCommandBuffer(Allocator.TempJob);
    ecb.Instantiate(prefab);

    ecb.Playback(_entityManager);
    ecb.Dispose();

    int count = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Speed)).CalculateEntityCount();
    Assert.AreEqual(2, count);
}
```

