## Assertions

### Preferred Assertions for EditMode

**Entity existence:**

```csharp
Assert.IsTrue(_entityManager.Exists(entity));
Assert.IsFalse(_entityManager.Exists(entity));
```

**Component presence:**

```csharp
Assert.IsTrue(_entityManager.HasComponent<Speed>(entity));
Assert.IsFalse(_entityManager.HasComponent<Speed>(entity));
```

**Value comparison:**

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(expected, actual);
Assert.AreNotEqual(unexpected, actual);
```

**Component data:**

```csharp
Speed speed = _entityManager.GetComponentData<Speed>(entity);
Assert.AreEqual(10f, speed.Value);
```

**Query results:**

```csharp
int count = _entityManager.CreateEntityQuery(typeof(Speed)).CalculateEntityCount();
Assert.AreEqual(expectedCount, count);
```

**Assertion messages:**

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(1, count, "Should create exactly one entity");
Assert.IsTrue(hasComponent, "Prefab must have Speed component");
```

## Test Maintenance

### EditMode Test Checklist

- [ ] All tests use `[Test]` (not `[UnityTest]`)
- [ ] World is properly disposed in `[TearDown]`
- [ ] NativeContainers are disposed
- [ ] No `yield return` statements
- [ ] No system execution (use PlayMode for that)
- [ ] ECB tests validate after playback
- [ ] Helper methods are reused
- [ ] Test names follow naming convention
- [ ] No hard-coded magic numbers
- [ ] Clear assertion messages

## Summary

**EditMode Tests:**

- Fast, synchronous unit tests
- Test components, queries, ECB logic in isolation
- Use `[Test]` attribute
- Always dispose World and NativeContainers
- Validate after ECB playback using queries
- Focus on component data and logic correctness
